  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "After annexing Southern Border immortals, Fang Yuan gains many immortal material resources. Among at least five or six resource points that can match his dragonfish business, Xia Cha grotto-heaven’s year essence pool is one of them.",
      "chapters": [
        1635
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "His most important gain from that annexation set is Xia Cha grotto-heaven’s year essence pool. In a previous life he did not know Xia Cha had one and built his own, wasting resources on a duplicate. In this life he takes over Xia Cha’s year essence pool directly and throws year beasts, ancient year beasts, and immemorial year beasts into it.",
      "chapters": [
        1790
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "year-essence-pool",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_xia_cha"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After annexing Xia Cha grotto-heaven, he gains a bunch of time path dao marks and the tributary of the River of Time becomes wider, so he can control the upper and lower limit of the rate of time to a greater extent. Xia Cha did not pass any myriad tribulations and had only seventy thousand time path dao marks.",
      "chapters": [
        1816
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
